{"id":"1dcab8a9c1b6bac87ab1c3ebf558cc99f5a1668ea28cf77c52bc1aa983c1e0c1","at":"2026-10-27T06:18:36Z","commit":"998c0d525899c5ec42dcd994805ea7deb62c6615","parents":["794b3749e754c0bda180e2e901917f8c1952a825098508efb96574f568f58dbb"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.Native.SessionsTest: the sections of spec 09: the session callbacks are Sessions' functions, and each honors :now at microsecond precision","hash":"210138f1"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/09-native-sessions.md#auth-sessions","hash":"6dcf01a5"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"09 intro: Native's callbacks equal Sessions.fetch/list results; a millisecond :now is kept as microsecond precision in created_at, last_used_at, inserted_at, a touch's last_used_at, by id too, and complete_step's updated_at (the bug fixed: a :now equal to the row's updated_at was replaced by the system clock); :now decides expiry by id","basis":"review"}
