{"id":"d2c761f39d4d14af109d94957b96906b83efd85c38b411fc3ed5cc1cd04d3ef8","at":"2026-10-27T06:19:04Z","commit":"998c0d525899c5ec42dcd994805ea7deb62c6615","parents":["7a9ccf9a44f181e7c327d0a55d5426352c439042621c3d3eb039c3b43bf6b49f"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.Native.ThrottleTest: the sections of spec 10: the keys: the normalized username or :invalid, the address as a string; the longer wait wins","hash":"4955ff31"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/10-native-throttle.md#auth-throttle-keys","hash":"7095414e"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"10 §1 prose: authenticate with \"Bea \", \"not a name!\" and \"@@\" from a tuple address writes {:user, \"bea\"}, {:user, :invalid} x2 and {:ip, \"192.0.2.70\"} x3; check/3 gives the longer of the two keys' waits; failure/3 counts on both keys at now; now/0 is the system clock in ms","basis":"review"}
