{"id":"008576988f069a1adeddb9a651abae4d00872e726679089a31b8e4a691207762","at":"2026-10-27T06:20:41Z","commit":"998c0d525899c5ec42dcd994805ea7deb62c6615","parents":["236ad2b44576ef3ed3b03beab6fd0153919fde6356cf46ea7cb00ae6c7f34af7"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.Native.UserCommandsTest: the sections of spec 13: bootstrap refuses a password among its words too; no answer repeats a password or a stray word","hash":"0cf9f2fa"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/13-native-users.md#auth-users-passwords","hash":"4ef000a6"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"UserCommands.bootstrap/3 refuses --password, --password= and -p with the exact \"never read\" message, and without the variable answers \"set THE_PASSWORD …\", making no user; the bootstrap, add and password answers don't contain their passwords; stray \"hunter2\" in add, password, disable, alone, and after bootstrap NAME are errors not containing it","basis":"review"}
{"id":"29db5b5971de307a457f7fa52777a3879dd7cc0b97bd8bb69bf74f5f6d0c63b5","at":"2026-10-27T06:20:43Z","commit":"998c0d525899c5ec42dcd994805ea7deb62c6615","parents":["7ad5303afba1e257721570e9837b7fe904f13a43b22550657ae6e513b038cd09"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.ClosedDefaultsTest: each setting that grants trust or loosens a policy grants nothing until it is set","hash":"1ef9c2f9"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/00-overview.md#auth-closed","hash":"3066fd04"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"each bullet of 00 §5 in its default state: Ldap.parse refuses plaintext without allow_plaintext and parses verify_peer true, refuses a bindless search without allow_anonymous_search; Provision refuses a local row (username_taken); the backend behavior has no user-making callback and bootstrap_admin is :exists once a user is; a --password word is refused and no user made; no Release env_prefix ships; require_role halts without membership and passes with it; no authorizer and authorize/3 false; log_in sets no remember cookie unless asked, and secure under https even given secure: false","basis":"review"}
{"id":"43d1050ff26aee04a44f8207eab2b2a4c3cd59bf06e26b89458272a353572665","at":"2026-10-27T06:21:04Z","commit":"998c0d525899c5ec42dcd994805ea7deb62c6615","parents":["e5bf221d4e7ed9e153f3f408fb9004101bd6293a83960e79516a66c0dff74921"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Auth.Authorizer","hash":"f8db49a5"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-contract.md#auth-authorize","hash":"b094edf2"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§9: the test configures the test authorizer (@behaviour Macaw.Auth.Authorizer) and Macaw.Auth.authorize/3 returns its callback's answer (an admin's :manage is true), read at each call (false again once the setting is deleted); a non-atom action or a non-User user is a FunctionClauseError. The behavior module is the one-callback contract the configured module implements","basis":"review","through":"config :macaw_auth, authorizer: Macaw.Auth.Test.Authorizer, a module implementing the Macaw.Auth.Authorizer behavior, whose authorize/3 callback Macaw.Auth.authorize/3 calls by the configured name"}
{"id":"b4199ea8e5aebe096dbcb93627e1266570dc9204bb019d154f79b7347db593c1","at":"2026-10-27T06:21:12Z","commit":"998c0d525899c5ec42dcd994805ea7deb62c6615","parents":[],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Auth.Conformance.__using__/1","hash":"bf3388ad"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-conformance.md#auth-kit","hash":"570634f4"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"04's intro states what use Macaw.Auth.Conformance does (backend: and fixtures: required, async: false, the backend set and reset before each test and put back after); __using__/1 is the macro that expands it","basis":"proposed"}
{"id":"6b5c2eeb76b31a6443fee36b127da823a1a8e4862638bee0c411e3ba0bcb7590","at":"2026-10-27T06:21:14Z","commit":"998c0d525899c5ec42dcd994805ea7deb62c6615","parents":["b4199ea8e5aebe096dbcb93627e1266570dc9204bb019d154f79b7347db593c1"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Auth.Conformance.__using__/1","hash":"bf3388ad"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-conformance.md#auth-kit","hash":"570634f4"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"04 intro: eval of a module using the kit without backend: or without fixtures: raises KeyError; the module's ExUnit config is async: false; the kit's setup (called via __ex_unit__(:setup, ...)) sets :backend to the backend under test and resets the store (a signed-in user is gone); on_exit puts back the configured backend, or deletes the setting when none was","basis":"review","through":"use Macaw.Auth.Conformance in the test module, which expands the kit's quote into it at compile time"}
